OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs1 wsj#57sj  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$ -,* %-.*,$%** %-& (,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAThree friends on their student
OL,4,Adebt: One paid off, one chipping away
OL,5,Aand one creeping up
OL,6,
OL,7,F"The conversation was just so much less
OL,8,Frelevant at that time," says Charlotte.
OL,9,F"As our careers have gone on and our
OL,10,Fpaths have diverged more and more...
OL,11,Fthose conversations start to come more
OL,12,Fto the forefront."
OL,14,FThe friends, now in their early 30s,
OL,15,Fwent to the University of Newcastle in
OL,16,Fthe same year tuition fees tripled to
OL,17,F#9,000 a year in England and Wales, and
OL,18,Fnew loans called Plan 2 were
OL,19,Fintroduced. Each borrowed about #37,500
OL,20,Fto cover three years of tuition and
OL,21,Fliving costs.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
